WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.717
-Today is Friday,
and that's usually

00:00:01.717 --> 00:00:04.033
when I catch up on
some personal stuff, you know?

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.701
I check my in-box,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.434
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:09.701
Now, I was --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.868
Well, I was running
a bit behind today,

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:15.267
so I thought --
I was busy today.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.567
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.234
I was trying to make all
my money back in scratch-offs.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:20.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:21.834
So, I thought,
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:23.133
I'd just like the write out
my weekly thank-you notes

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.667
right now --
is that cool with you guys?

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Aww.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.767
-You're the best. Thank you.
Thank you very much.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:28.868
James, can I get some

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.434
thank-you-note writing music,
please?

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.067
♪♪

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.601
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.901
-Wow!

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:41.167
-Thank you, New Mexico,

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.133
legalizing
recreational marijuana.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.467
Or as stoners put it,

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.634
"Wait, there's a New Mexico?"

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:47.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.234
[ Applause ]

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.467
♪♪

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.434
Thank you, Costco,

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.200
for bringing back free samples
to your stores.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.667
Because if the pandemic
has taught me one thing,

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.067
it's that I should eat loose
meat from strangers' hands.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.434
-Aww.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:08.634
[ Applause ]
Aww! That's sweet.

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.901
So sweet.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:12.901
-Sweet meat.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.234
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.067
♪♪

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:20.334
Thank you, the new speakeasy in
New York City's subway station.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.534
Usually,
if I want to see someone

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.534
secretly drink alcohol
in the subway system,

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.601
I have to ride the subway.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.501
[ Applause ]
And I don't.

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.367
-Secretly.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:31.801
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.267
♪♪

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:38.234
-Thank you, Red Lobster's
new Codzilla fish sandwich

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:39.501
for sounding
a lot more appetizing

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:42.033
than Arby's
Kongrilla nuggets.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:44.367
-Oh!

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.934
-It sounds like
a male exotic dancer.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.601
[ Laughter ]
"I'll have a sack of nuggets."

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:52.167
-"Coming to the stage...
Codzilla."

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.467
♪♪

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:56.400
-Thank you, Uber CEO,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.400
saying the company
may soon deliver weed.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.968
Or as Papa John's drivers
put it,

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.400
"Hey, that's our thing."

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:08.400
♪ Well, you're too hot to trot,
now, baby ♪

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.801
♪♪

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.300
♪ Too hot to stop ♪

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.734
Whoo!

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.334
♪♪

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.133
[ Music ends ]

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:18.200
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.767
♪♪

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:24.033
-Thank you, new dog park
with a bar opening in Buffalo.

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.667
Or as dogs put it,

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:28.067
"Whatever you need on justify
your problem, Glenn."

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.300
"Whatever you need, bud."

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.901
-"Whatever, man."

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.167
-Oh, oh.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.701
♪♪

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:40.968
-Thank you, new high-alcohol
White Claw Surge,

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.167
for answering the question,

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:44.701
what if LaCroix
made you throw up and cry?

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.767
-True.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:50.934
-Oh.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:52.334
♪♪

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.934
-Thank you, condiments,
for always looking like

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:57.567
you're having a party
on my refrigerator's balcony.

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.300
-♪ Too hot to trot ♪

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:04.734
-Mnh!

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:05.767
Well...

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:07.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.901
That's just --
That's my jam, that song.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.534
-Yeah, that's it.
That's a great song.

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:14.300
♪ Well, you're too hot to trot,
now, baby ♪

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.300
-Whoo!
-Whoo!

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.300
-Unh!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.434
♪ Too hot to stop ♪

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:18.701
-Whoo!
-Whoo!

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.367
♪♪

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:23.200
-Is it, "Too hot to trot,"
and then...

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.501
-"Too hot to stop."
-"Too hot to stop."

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:25.634
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:26.901
-'Cause you're trotting.
And then, you're --

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:29.234
you know, you can't stop.
-That's a jam.

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:30.667
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.067
[ Chuckles ]
-Is this the last one?

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.567
-What's that?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.067
-Is that the last
thank-you note?

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:39.267
-Uh. Yeah, sure.
'Cause it looks like it, right?

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:40.968
-Yeah. That's nice, sweet.
-Yeah, it's cool.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.334
-I like it.
-Man.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.767
-I like how you thank people.
I think it's a good attitude.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.434
-Yeah?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:49.601
-Hold on a second.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.067
"Unplug Higgins' microphone."

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.901
Send.
[ Feedback whines ]

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.000
-Wha-- Hey --

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.400
I didn't --

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.501
[ No audio ]

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:03.033
Ub-- Ah--

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:04.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:07.234
Ah -- Ah -- Ah --

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:10.100
-Just turn it back on.
Turn it back on.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.267
-A big bowl of Dick's.
-Oh, okay, alright, alright.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.234
Hey.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:15.968
Hey, is he talking
about the coupon cards?

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.501
-Yeah, the coupon cards
from Dick's Sporting Goods.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:18.801
-The coupons from
Dick's Sporting Goods.

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.033
-Yeah. They're giving them away.
-Yeah, I know, I know.

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:21.434
But then, you couldn't --
we couldn't hear

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.167
what you were saying --
the microphone was cutting out.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.300
-Why was the microphone
cutting out?

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.801
-I don't know.
I'm sorry.

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.434
-It's like a big grab offer --
grab as many Dick's as you can.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:30.100
-I know. I know. Everyone --
Yeah, I gotcha. Gotcha. Got--

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.000
You either got to either put
his mic on or turn it off.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.834
-I love that store.
Love that store.

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:36.033
-You got to mic on
or turn his mic off.

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:37.400
It's one or the other.
Sorry.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.033
-Alright. It's on?
[ Claps twice ]

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:41.434
[ Speaking rhythmically ]
Mic on.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.901
[ Laughter ]
-Mm.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.467
♪♪

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.267
-Thank you, hanging plants,

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:49.000
or as I like to call you,
"decorative jellyfish."

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.801
They're you go, everybody.
Those are our thank-you notes.

